FIGURE's patch 3 of 3 to ImGuizmo (commit 105e4fde45e4e74aae8973d98750820ef7aca7e2).

ImGradient::Edit kept the selected point and the point being moved in function statics and drew into a child
window of the fixed id 137: two editors shared one selection and one drag (a drag in one moved the point of the same
index in the other), two editors in one window drew into one child, and a press on a point, which no item took,
started moving the window. The child's id now comes from the ID stack (ImGui::GetID), the selection and the moved
point are kept in the window's storage under ids derived from it, and an invisible button under the points takes the
press. Applied to third_party/ImGuizmo/ImGradient.cpp; checked by src/tests/figure_test_gizmo.F90 (a stop dragged,
the window not moved). To offer upstream.

--- a/ImGradient.cpp
+++ b/ImGradient.cpp
